<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <Sdk Name="Cosmos.Sdk" />

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
    <!-- Without Storage the built-in NVMe driver is never brought up, which
         leaves the nvme cell's controller free for the suite's own NVMe
         drivers. Nothing else in the suite needs Storage; USB, which the
         usb-mouse cell needs, stays on because Keyboard does. Network and
         Mouse must stay on too: the suite's drivers publish a network link,
         which the rtl8139 cells take a DHCP lease through, and mice. -->
    <CosmosEnableStorage>false</CosmosEnableStorage>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!--
    One cell per piece of hardware a user driver will bind, none of which a
    built-in driver claims: QEMU's edu test device and an RTL8139 NIC on both
    arches, an 82574L (e1000e) on arm64 only, since the E1000E built-in takes
    it on x64, a USB mouse behind an xHCI controller with no USB stick, and
    an NVMe controller, free because this kernel builds without Storage.
    Definitions live in tests/profiles.json.

    The gic* modifiers are arm64-only and apply to every profile, which gives
    the e1000e and nvme cells their GICv3 run (MSI-X through the ITS) and
    GICv2 run (polled), and the USB mouse both interrupt paths (xHCI MSI-X
    on GICv3, polled on GICv2). x64 = 4 cells; arm64 = 5 profiles x
    {bare, gicv2, gicv3} = 15 cells.
  -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <CosmosTestProfile Include="edu" />
    <CosmosTestProfile Include="rtl8139" />
    <CosmosTestProfile Include="e1000e-arm64" />
    <CosmosTestProfile Include="usb-mouse" />
    <CosmosTestProfile Include="nvme" />
    <CosmosTestModifier Include="gicv2" />
    <CosmosTestModifier Include="gicv3" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Core kernel packages (using project references for development) -->
  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="../../../src/Cosmos.Kernel/Cosmos.Kernel.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../../../src/Cosmos.Kernel.System/Cosmos.Kernel.System.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="../../Cosmos.TestRunner.Framework/Cosmos.TestRunner.Framework.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <!-- Architecture-specific HAL (using project references for development) -->
  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(DefineConstants)' != '' AND $(DefineConstants.Contains('ARCH_X64'))">
    <ProjectReference Include="../../../src/Cosmos.Kernel.HAL.X64/Cosmos.Kernel.HAL.X64.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup Condition="'$(DefineConstants)' != '' AND $(DefineConstants.Contains('ARCH_ARM64'))">
    <ProjectReference Include="../../../src/Cosmos.Kernel.HAL.ARM64/Cosmos.Kernel.HAL.ARM64.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
